b-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":115,"digest":"sha256:c6d9001ab034eaf50d2e0692d07b444489fe634d6f782e72d8f8c495a317c531","download_count":2,"created_at":"2026-10-29T20:15:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T20:15:45Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/YOLOW92/pagesift/releases/download/v0.81.2/pagesift-v0.81.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz.sha256"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/YOLOW92/pagesift/tarball/v0.81.2","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/YOLOW92/pagesift/zipball/v0.81.2","body":"# PageSift 0.81.2 Release Notes: Zero Content Loss for Adaptive Upgrades\n\n> **Release Version**: `v0.81.2`\n> **Release Date**: 2026-10-30\n> **License**: AGPL-3.0-only (Commercial licensing available)\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\n0.81.1 stopped `engine: auto` browser upgrades when the extracted content stopped improving. That\nremoved the tail latency of JavaScript shells and challenge pages, but one class of page lost\ncontent: a page whose HTTP body is a bare client-side redirect and whose target only becomes\nreadable after its scripts run. The browser was stopped before the target content appeared, so the\nHTTP result (empty) was returned.\n\n0.81.2 keeps the adaptive stop and adds a content-first path for those redirect pages:\n\n- **Content appears, capture immediately.** For a bare redirect page, the browser is polled for\n  the first non-empty main frame; the DOM is captured and extracted as soon as content appears,\n  without waiting for `DOMContentLoaded` or network idle.\n- **Relative patience.** The wait is bounded by the page's own HTTP fetch time and the caller's\n  total timeout, not by a fixed number of seconds. If no content appears, the HTTP result is\n  returned as before.\n- **No change for normal pages.** The adaptive probe, early stop and HTTP fallback from 0.81.1 are\n  unchanged. Explicit `engine: browser` is still uncapped.\n\n## Measurements\n\nLocal A2 replay, 269 pages, same per-URL process model as the 0.81 report:\n\n| Version | 1 worker | 16 workers | Extracted characters |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| 0.81.0 | 110.7 s / 2.4 pages/s | 21.9 s / 12.3 pages/s | 2,376,184 |\n| 0.81.2 | **88.0 s / 3.1 pages/s** | **13.5 s / 20.0 pages/s** | **2,376,358** |\n\nPer-page comparison against 0.81.0: **zero pages lose content**. The redirect page that motivated\nthis release returns 476 characters instead of 405, and its wall time falls from 17.0 s to 9.4 s.\nThe total is +174 characters.\n\n0.81.1 was faster on this replay (85.7 s / 10.5 s) but returned 301 fewer characters overall\nbecause it dropped that redirect page's content. 0.81.2 deliberately spends a few seconds on that\npage to keep the zero-loss guarantee; it remains 1.26× faster than 0.81.0 at one worker and 1.62×\nfaster at 16 workers.\n\n## Behaviour changes\n\n- A bare client-side redirect with no HTTP content now waits for its target's first content and\n  captures it immediately. If the target never produces content, the HTTP result is returned with\n  the same fallback warnings as 0.81.1.\n- No configuration or API changes.\n\n"}